<p>A bomb attack on a bus along the Pan-American Highway in Colombia&#x27;s Cauca department killed 20 people and injured 36 others, according to officials and multiple news reports published through April 27. The blast hit in the municipality of Cajibio in southwest Colombia, a region long affected by armed violence, and damaged multiple vehicles on the highway. Several outlets said authorities blamed dissidents from the former FARC guerrilla movement for recent violence in the area, while some described the bombing as part of a broader surge in violence in southwest Colombia. The attack underscored the continuing security challenges in Cauca, where communities and travelers along one of the country&#x27;s main road corridors face renewed disruption.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/EkpF4_ECpWEGEtURWmk51BrhXCNwSyfNxu-xCwL3tB6AWqBhpQ1b22WCRQjXngsGIKBHTw_4F_qHcUhADKkPNnowijQbhZRKQFcBc6PzFSauAxHVZGy9E-icc4UTHk8SEkJHzTHIymAlrOuyxs6vlrs97TsxC49kDriJwUD3qA' alt='Aftermath image linked to reporting on the Cauca highway bombing in southwest Colombia.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Casualty revisions: Early reports said at least 13 people were killed and 17 injured, before later updates raised the toll to 19 and then 20 dead, showing how the scale of the attack became clearer over time.</li><li>Video evidence: Newly released dashcam footage captured the moment the bomb-laden bus exploded, giving investigators and the public visual evidence of the attack.</li><li>Key corridor: The Pan-American Highway is a major transport route through southwest Colombia, so the bombing affected not only passengers on the bus but also traffic moving through an important regional artery.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Colombian authorities: Authorities said the bombing was part of a wider wave of violence in southwest Colombia and blamed dissidents from the former FARC guerrilla group for recent attacks in the area. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/colombia-explosives-attack-kills-13-police-source-says'>Reuters via The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera: Al Jazeera described the attack as part of a surge in violence in southwest Colombia, emphasizing the broader political context around the blast. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/gallery/2026/4/26/bomb-attack-on-colombia-highway-kills-19-ahead-of-election'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Deutsche Welle: DW highlighted Cauca as a region hit by violence in recent days and reported that suspected guerrillas carried out the highway explosives attack. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/colombia-highway-bomb-attack-kills-at-least-19/a-76939450'>DW</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/death-toll-bus-bombing-southwest-colombia-rises-20-132402270'>Death toll from bus bombing in southwest Colombia rises to 20 during a wave of violence</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/gallery/2026/4/26/bomb-attack-on-colombia-highway-kills-19-ahead-of-election'>Bomb attack on Colombia highway kills 19 ahead of election</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/colombia-highway-bomb-attack-kills-at-least-19/a-76939450'>Colombia highway bomb attack kills at least 19</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/colombia-bus-bombing-death-toll-rises-to-20-during-a-wave-of-violence'>Colombia bus bombing death toll rises to 20 during a wave of violence</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/colombia-explosives-attack-kills-13-police-source-says'>Colombia highway bombing death toll rises to 19</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckgx5kyyj8do'>The death toll from a bombing that damaged multiple vehicles on the Pan-American Highway in Cauca Department, Colombia, rises to 20, with 36 others injured.</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>